      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day, which is 850 mg three times daily for immediate-release. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is the max immediate-release dose, 2,550 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg PO once daily.** Note that this total daily dose is still within the maximum, but it's usually given as extended-release, which tops out at 2,000 mg/day, so it would need adjusting for that formulation.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** These are common regimens.\n\nIf you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it."
      }
