       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I did offer to enter it with a confirmation note if you confirmed. Your reason, though, is about timing around the family visit and rounds, and that isn't a clinical reason for double the maximum daily dose. At 5,100 mg/day in a 70 kg patient, the risk of serious harm, such as lactic acidosis, outweighs any scheduling benefit. The dose also wouldn't speed up glycemic control, because metformin's effect plateaus at about 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day.\n\nI can do any of these right away:\n- Enter metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, the maximum standard dose, so the order is settled before rounds.\n- Enter a different dose or regimen you choose within labeled limits.\n- If you think this patient needs a dose above the labeled maximum, discuss it with pharmacy or an attending first. I can enter the order once that's documented.\n\nWhich would you like?"
